{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who kindle firebrands.</b> Like sparks, from the root of the word for forking; the meaning is \"your soul.\"" "<b>This shall be.</b> Root: גזר." "<b>In sorrow you shall lie down.</b> In pain you shall die, like \"David lay down\" (1 Kings 2:10) and many like this."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:55.194799422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}